"""Cooperative fail-closed guard for finalized v2 ref transactions.

This checker is intentionally tree-ish based.  The reference-transaction hook
invokes it for the candidate commit, so ``git commit --no-verify`` cannot turn
an accidental unreviewed finalized shard into repository history while the
checkout keeps its canonical hooksPath.  Its identity and receipt are public
integrity binds, not authority: a caller that disables hooks or forges the
environment can bypass them.  The official consumer therefore invokes this
checker inside its already authenticated closure immediately before update-ref.
"""

